    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p15-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Calculate the mean and population standard deviation for these scores. Answer correct to one decimal place.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Mean $=14.3$, $\\sigma=3.3$.",
          "worked": "There are $16$ scores, with $\\sum x=229$ and $\\sum x^2=3451$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\mu&=\\frac{229}{16}\\\\\\mu&=14.3125\\\\\\mu&\\approx14.3\\\\\\sigma&=\\sqrt{\\frac{3451}{16}-\\left(\\frac{229}{16}\\right)^2}\\\\\\sigma&\\approx3.3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "What is the z-score of the student who scored the lowest on the test? Answer to 1 d.p.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-1.9$",
          "worked": "The lowest score is $8$. Using the unrounded population standard deviation from part a:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}z&=\\frac{x-\\mu}{\\sigma}\\\\z&=\\frac{8-14.3125}{\\sqrt{2775}/16}\\\\z&\\approx-1.9\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q12-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Lucy was absent for this task, but her mark is usually 1.5 standard deviations above the mean. What mark should her teacher give her as an estimate? Answer to 2 decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$19.25$ marks out of $20$.",
          "worked": "Lucy has $z=1.5$. Using the unrounded population statistics:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\mu+z\\sigma\\\\x&=14.3125+1.5\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2775}}{16}\\right)\\\\x&\\approx19.25\\end{align*}$$\n\nHer estimated mark is $19.25$ out of $20$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      }
    ]
  },
